Package: resurgam-lab-agent
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, proxmox-backup-client, qemu-server, qemu-utils
Description: RESURGAM Recovery Lab probe agent
 Installed on a PVE cluster designated for Recovery Lab use (manifest
 EPIC 10, ADR 0019). Polls RESURGAM's backend over an outbound-only
 HTTPS backchannel for Application Group members ready to test, maps
 each one's PBS snapshot directly as a local block device
 (`proxmox-backup-client map` -- zero-copy, no restore), overlays a
 writable COW layer so the guest can boot without ever touching the
 real backup image, and starts a VM around it via `qm` -- proving a
 backup's recoverability without paying the cost of a full restore.
 .
 Never opens an inbound port and never touches the RESURGAM database
 directly; the only network paths it needs are outbound HTTPS to the
 RESURGAM backend and outbound access to its own locally-configured PBS
 instance(s) on port 8007.
 .
 Also carries the write-side of a second Phase B responsibility: this
 same host writes each Lab run's probe appliance cloud-init snippet to
 local disk, since PVE has no REST endpoint to upload one (confirmed
 live 2026-09-21).

Package: resurgam-lab-prober
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, iproute2, iputils-ping, dnsmasq, nftables, nmap
Description: RESURGAM Recovery Lab probe appliance
 Recovery Lab's per-run probe appliance (manifest EPIC 10, ADR 0019,
 Phase B) -- cloned fresh for each Lab run, dual-homed onto the run's
 isolated PVE SDN Lab VNet (net0) and an existing uplink bridge (net1).
 Acts as that VNet's own router/DHCP server/firewall/SNAT gateway
 (dnsmasq + nftables, entirely self-contained in this VM -- PVE itself
 never provisions a subnet on the Lab VNet), and runs the 3-tier probe
 hierarchy's Level 2 (`icmp`/`arp`) and Level 3 (`tcp_port`/`http`/
 `https`/`dns`/`tls_handshake`/`ssh_banner`/`nmap_scan`) checks against
 each restored member over that segment, reporting results back to
 RESURGAM's backend over its own outbound HTTPS path (net1).
